   "widgets_values": [
    "WIDE-SHOT FACE FIX\n\nWhy wide-shot faces go mushy in H3: the DiT draws in 32x32 px tokens (16x VAE + 2x2 patch). A 35 px face in a 1024x576 wide shot is ~2 tokens, so eyes and mouth have nowhere to go. Higher output resolution barely helps (the face is still a tiny share of the frame).\nH3 Face Atlas finds every anime face (ONNX detector, CPU), tracks it per shot, and magnifies each one into its own 512 px tile of ONE canvas: ~60 tokens per face instead of ~2, all characters in a single pass. The whole frame sits above the tiles at half size, pinned (not redrawn), so the faces are redrawn while seeing the scene: no stray effects pasted onto faces and no extra boiling. Pass 1's audio is pinned, so mouths follow the dialogue.\nUse the SAME prompt + style LoRA as the render. Faces already big on screen are skipped (close-ups pass through untouched)."
   ]
